# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution): at 188 rad/s (300 mm/s) something fails; hv0.sim_dist,
# zeroed then, is how far the axis went (1 rad = 1.59 mm). Coasting takes
# ~16 rad (26 mm) and ~180 ms.
# The link to LinuxCNC is lost: the link component times out, drops enable
# and flags CMD error; fault0 (cmd_stop = 1) runs the quick stop: qstop0
# brakes on an S-curve trajectory at 30 % of what the motor can do, then
# the outputs go off (~2 rad, 3 mm). The drive's velocity observer lags at
# that deceleration, so the stop rings a little before it settles.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 300
run 1
hv0.sim_vel
hv0.sim_dist = 0
lcncstop
run 0.008
fault0.stop
run 0.3
hv0.sim_dist
hv0.sim_vel
fault0.fault
fault0.state
fault0.en_out
fault0.stop
@expect hv0.sim_vel[1] ~ 188.5 1%
@expect fault0.stop[1] == 1
@expect hv0.sim_dist ~ 2 0.5
@expect hv0.sim_vel[2] ~ 0 0.5
@expect fault0.fault == 1
@expect fault0.state == 3
@expect fault0.en_out == 0
@expect fault0.stop[2] == 0
